{"ts":"2026-07-07T07:01:56.726Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Context\nThe noun-verb consolidation (pm-n7rr, ADR pm-pbyu) keeps every legacy spelling alive as a hidden alias via the shim layer (pm-0z7n), and the v1.0 GA stability contract (pm-agou) will eventually freeze the grammar and decide which aliases can be retired. Today there is no way to know whether any agent or script still uses a given deprecated spelling — removal decisions would be guesses, and a wrong guess breaks working automations for zero benefit.\n\n## Proposal\nInstrument alias resolution with the existing local telemetry subsystem (counters only, no new infrastructure, same privacy posture — local-only, never in git):\n- The alias shim increments a per-alias counter (alias -> canonical, count, last_seen) whenever a deprecated spelling is resolved.\n- Surface the rollup in the diagnostics noun (ops stats / telemetry stats): aliases still in use, counts over the retention window, and aliases with zero recorded use.\n- Document the removal criterion in the ADR: an alias is removable at a major boundary only after N releases with zero recorded use across reporting workspaces (exact N decided in pm-agou).\n\n## Scope guard\nCounting happens inside the shim resolution path only — canonical spellings cost nothing. No network, no new storage format: reuse the telemetry store and its existing disable env-vars."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-0mox"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Alias-usage counters: measure deprecated-spelling hits so grammar-freeze removals are evidence-based"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":""},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","cli-simplification","telemetry"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-07T07:01:56.726Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-07T07:01:56.726Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"maintainer-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Alias shim records per-alias hit counters (alias, canonical, count, last_seen) in the local telemetry store honoring existing telemetry disable env-vars; canonical spellings incur zero overhead; a diagnostics surface lists alias usage and zero-use aliases; the deprecation ADR documents the zero-use-for-N-releases removal criterion; unit test proves counter increment on alias resolution and absence on canonical invocation"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-n7rr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-0z7n","kind":"blocked_by","created_at":"2026-07-07T07:01:56.726Z"},{"id":"pm-agou","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-07T07:01:56.726Z"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a7233fd18b08759353d482b023dde7fab4926e3e9789833994f8e7a5e0cb10cb","message":""}
